silicon-control (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Intel backend (expected: tested on simulated hardware only): PL1/PL2
    through powercap, the temperature limit through the TCC offset, turbo
    through intel_pstate; warnings for thermald and for an old Raptor Lake
    microcode. No undervolt on Intel (set it in the BIOS).
  * The stock value is always within the GUI's ranges.

 -- senseikiritof <tonifede98@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:29:32 +0200

silicon-control (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Generic backend where the AMD one does not apply (Intel, ARM, the AMD
    families not in the table, HX laptops) or with the kernel parameter
    siliconctl.generic: FMax through cpufreq, boost, power profile, fans, the
    CPU temperature and the package power; never an SMU command.
  * The GUI shows what the CPU reports; the Monitor shows its values as soon as
    it opens.

 -- senseikiritof <tonifede98@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:18:21 +0200

silicon-control (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Silicon Control: Ryzen Control 0.8.0 under the new name (helper
    siliconctl, GUI silicon-control); AMD Ryzen only so far.
  * Takes over from Ryzen Control: replaces the ryzen-control package and
    imports its settings, profiles, calibrations, crash-guard markers and
    trust rule; the login entry and GUI preferences at the first start of the
    GUI; ryzenctl.off still honoured.

 -- senseikiritof <tonifede98@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:12:14 +0200
